DCU had me really worried there for a  minute assault on our co2 say that I was  nervous going into this one is a bit of  an understatement I had some pretty  major issues with Justice League war and  I flat out hated son of Batman so even  though I knew going in that this was not  part of that same continuity that  they're now building based off the new  52 I was still just flat-out nervous  because I was afraid DC animated movies  just had lost their mojo altogether  what a relief for me because this movie  is a total blast now I do feel the need  to point out that the full title Batman  assault on Arkham is a little bit of a  misnomer because Batman himself he's not  the focus on this he's around and it's  certainly it's set in his world and it's  dealing with a lot of his rogues gallery  but he himself he's not the focus but  really it's only the title that plays a  little bit of this bait-and-switch  because once you're into the film itself  it's very clear very early on as to who  the actual heroes of this story are now  in this case I use the term heroes very  loosely so here's your basic set up  Amanda Waller is a government operative  involved in some very shady stuff now  when the Riddler gets caught and jailed  for about the 500th times it turns out  that he had in his possession something  that Amanda Waller needs back that  MacGuffin is now in the property vault  at Arkham Asylum so Amanda Waller  assembles the latest version of The  Suicide Squad which is made up of  various convicts and not nice people to  go in and get it back this particular  iteration of the Suicide Squad is made  up of Deadshot king shark black spider  Captain Boomerang killer frost  cagey beast and Harley Quinn through  some really nice minimal use of  exposition the film establishes very  early on that some of these guys have  been in the situation and made part of  the Suicide Squad before some of them  it's completely new and they're being  brought in on this on the firt for the  first time the ones who get the most  focus are Deadshot and Harley Quinn and  if I'm being completely honest black  spider and cagey beast there I kind of  throw always a little bit but the other  three get some really nice moments and  some really nice to mention to them so  overall it's pretty well-balanced  how large the team is and this thing is  just a rollercoaster of a movie right at  the beginning every single member of the  team gets their own little sort of  opening segment to show who they are  what they're about and I'll give you a  little bit of a sense of you know their  fighting style of what it is they kind  of bring to the proceedings as part of  this team  there is plenty of action in this thing  and like I said since they've all got  different fight styles and ways of going  about combat  it keeps the action scenes from becoming  boring even though there's quite a few  of them offering one coming right after  another but it never gets overloaded it  stays well paced and given that these  heroes are well to put it bluntly they  are not nice people things do get quite  a bit violent at times but the thing is  in this case because of the nature of  these characters and their criminal  backgrounds and everything else it makes  sense that things are gonna get a bit  bloodier and a bit Messier as opposed to  say son of Batman where it was  completely gratuitous and there wasn't  really a point to how violent in god  voice working this thing is top-notch  this is taking place in the same  universe as the Arkham series of video  games which means we get some old pros  coming back into the mix namely we get  Kevin Conroy as Batman and we get CCH  pounder as Amanda Waller now we do get a  couple of replacement voices for some  established characters and they're  effectively brought in to give  impersonations of the best-known  versions of these characters  specifically we get this with Harley  Quinn and the Joker I normally would  have considered it a spoiler to mention  the Joker but the thing set in Arkham  you know he's at least going to appear  and the thing is on paper I'm not a huge  fan of the idea of actually being  brought in basically just to do an  impression of the last person who did it  as opposed to having the freedom to do  their own thing but honestly if the  results are gonna be this good I will  take it and be very happy with it  me I got a hand it out to hynden walch  and Troy Baker who are doing spot-on  impersonations of the work done by  Arleen Sorkin and Mark Hamill is Harley  Quinn in the Joker they might as well be  the real deal  rest of the voice cast all solid work  like the only one that threw me off a  little bit was Nolan North Scott nee  penguin I could have done with that but  he hardly drank things down and it was a  cameo appearance at that which brings me  to the other thing which is that I  really  how batman's better-known robes gallery  is sort of sprinkled across the film  they never take it over it's never about  them but given that it's set in Arkham  which houses so many of these well-known  characters characters much better known  than any member of The Suicide Squad it  really would have felt like a missed  opportunity if we didn't at least see  them and I like the ones that we see I  like the way in which they're used for  their little appearances it just it  feels like oh yeah cool but again they  never take over the film and it stays  properly focused I really I just had a  ton of fun with this thing and the only  complaints I have they're really  nitpicks yes Amanda Waller loses some of  her ambiguity and she's a bit more  straight-up villain than she normally is  but honestly given the nature of this  particular story I'm not sure there was  a way around that there's also a  surprising amount of near nudity on the  part of both female members of the  Suicide Squad which I kind of could've  done without but what I will say is we  are at these given reasons for why these  things are happening granted their  flimsy reasons sometimes but it's a heck  of a lot more than we got if as far as  explanation goes compared to say for  instance Talia al Ghul's outfit in son  of Batman which defied all combat  practicality as well as the laws of  physics so coming out of this I am  honestly I'm just relieved it's just  such a load off my mind to know that DC  animated movies can still be good now  the continuity being set with the new  ones which is the next film we're gonna  get with the throne of Atlantis I'm  really nervous about that because that  continuity needs to get better and it  needs to get better soon but if I've got  to slog through those in order to get  gems like this I'll do it I'll complain  about it but I'll do it in the spirit of  the Suicide Squad who's your favorite  b-list comic book villain you know what  you don't even have to give a DC one I  personally I've always had a soft spot  for Spider Man's doppelganger so whoever  is your favorite b lister drop something  down in the comments let's talk about it  as for me I'll be back as soon as I get  my next fix
 

